1. ERR_EMPTY_RESPONSE – http://localhost:9090
        Cause: Prometheus container not reachable or app not exposing metrics.

2. Flask server only on 127.0.0.1 inside Docker
        Warning about serving on 127.0.0.1 vs 0.0.0.0
        Fix: Use host="0.0.0.0" in Flask app.
3. Prometheus YAML parsing error
        cannot unmarshal !!str 'targets...'
        Cause: Incorrect indentation or brackets in prometheus.yml.
4. Docker Compose volume mount errors
        Not a directory: Are you trying to mount a directory onto a file (or vice-versa)?
        Cause: Path mismatch, file vs folder confusion.
5. Grafana dashboard confusion
        “Where is Add new panel?”
        GUI terminology changed: use “Add panel” in new dashboard.
6. Alertmanager unreachable
        localhost:9093 cannot be reached
        Cause: Container not running or port mapping incorrect.
7. Docker Compose warnings
        version is obsolete, will be ignored
8. Git push 403 Forbidden
        Permission denied to your GitHub repo
        Cause: Wrong credentials or missing PAT.
9. Docker image pull timeout
        TLS handshake timeout when pulling Grafana image
10. Multiple Docker run conflicts
        Running multiple containers on same ports caused “address already in use”.
11. Prometheus alert rule syntax confusion
        Using increase(app_requests_total[1m]) > 5 incorrectly or testing too short interval caused no alerts to fire.
12. Alertmanager cluster gossip messages
        gossip not settled / gossip settled
        Normal info but confusing for first-time users.
13. Prometheus metrics not increasing
        Visiting / in Flask app sometimes before Prometheus scrape caused zero metrics.
14. Docker Compose mapping errors with spaces in folder path
        D:\Devops practice\SRE project 1\prometheus\alertmanager.yml
        Spaces in Windows paths can break volume mount if not quoted.


